 "notes": "Boulder City, three pinnacles of granite boulders on a sand bottom in the southern Similans, with sand gaps of 30-40 m between the pinnacles (Similan Dive Center); the northern pinnacle tops out at about 14 m, the middle one at 12 m and the southern one at 18 m, with sand at 25-30 m and the bottom past 35-40 m (IDC Phuket), and the mooring line is on the west side down to about 18 m. No OpenStreetMap feature exists; the position is estimated 400 m south-east of the end of Shark Fin Reef as the dive guides describe, so it is uncertain. The site coordinates (8.54, 97.64) were 4 km north-west, near Island 4.",
